scores.c: rename a local variable that ncurses' term.h claims as a macro.

FreeLinX builds tetris against ncurses 6.5 from build/deps/ncurses, and that
term.h renames its accessor to keep it out of the global namespace:

  #define numnames   NCURSES_PUBLIC_VAR(numnames())
  #define NCURSES_PUBLIC_VAR(name) _nc_##name

so the macro applies to identifiers, not only to uses.  checkscores() has an
`int numnames` and the preprocessor rewrites the declaration too:

  scores.c:778:15: error: conflicting types for '_nc_numnames'
    778 |         int i, j, k, numnames;
         |                      ^
  term.h:773:20: note: expanded from macro 'numnames'
  ncurses_dll.h:68:34: note: expanded from macro 'NCURSES_PUBLIC_VAR'
    68 | #define NCURSES_PUBLIC_VAR(name) _nc_##name
  term.h:763:1: note: previous declaration is here

ncurses' macro exists so that a program calling numnames() gets a function and
not the library's own variable.  tetris never calls it, so the macro is pure
cost here.  Rename the local to what it counts - the distinct names among the
high scores - and the collision is gone without -Dunnumames=..., which would
also have renamed the ncurses accessor wherever it is used.
